From 7b571006ba3b606fd4a1c00b4fdc6e5294feab99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 03:05:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] QuadratureDataLayout: fixes of the review, layout tests of
 the other integrators

- The environment variable `MFEM_MGIS_QUADRATURE_DATA_LAYOUT` is only read
  when the parameter `QuadratureDataLayout` is not given, as for the other
  parameters: an invalid value of the variable no longer stops a problem
  or a point-wise model which gives the parameter.
- The parameter of a problem is checked even without the multi-material
  integrator.
- The generators registered with the deprecated signature report that
  they do not support the component by component layout, instead of "no
  parameter expected".
- The generator of the transient heat transfer is written as the other
  ones (`noexcept`, `make_unique` with the context).
- User guide: values given directly to MGIS for a variable with several
  components follow the layout of the material; the prediction is
  refused when it uses the linearized operators. CHANGELOG.
- `HeatTransferKernelsTest` and `MicromorphicKernelsTest`: each
  computation by kernels is also made with the component by component
  layout, same results to the last bit in sequential on the host, to the
  tolerance of the test otherwise. The states are read through the views
  of MGIS.
- `BatchIntegrationTest`: refusal of the linearized operators, of the
  resultant force on a boundary and of a direct call of an element method;
  invalid value and precedence of the environment variable; layout of a
  point-wise model; names of the layout comparisons.
---
